Let 𝐺1 and 𝐺2 be groups, and let 𝜑 ∶ 𝐺1 → 𝐺2 be a homomorphism. Then

(1) the kernel of 𝜑, ker 𝜑 = {𝑥 ∈ 𝐺1 ∣ 𝜑(𝑥) = 𝑒2 }, where 𝑒2 is the identity element in 𝐺2 , is  a normal subgroup of 𝐺1 ;

(2) the image of 𝜑, im 𝜑 = {𝑦 ∈ 𝐺2 ∣ there is an 𝑥 ∈ 𝐺1 such that 𝜑(𝑥) = 𝑦} is a subgroup  of 𝐺2 .
